    {
      "id": "py-locals-get-kind",
      "name": "_PyLocals_GetKind",
      "category": "pycore_code",
      "signature": "_PyLocals_GetKind(Kinds, I)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Kinds",
          "type": "PyObject*"
        },
        {
          "name": "I",
          "type": "Int"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "_PyLocals_Kind",
      "docs": "\"Locals plus\" for a code object is the set of locals + cell vars +\nfree vars.  This relates to variable names as well as offsets into\nthe \"fast locals\" storage array of execution frames.  The compiler\nbuilds the list of names, their offsets, and the corresponding\nkind of local.\nThose kinds represent the source of the initial value and the\nvariable's scope (as related to closures).  A \"local\" is an\nargument or other variable defined in the current scope.  A \"free\"\nvariable is one that is defined in an outer scope and comes from\nthe function's closure.  A \"cell\" variable is a local that escapes\ninto an inner function as part of a closure, and thus must be\nwrapped in a cell.  Any \"local\" can also be a \"cell\", but the\n\"free\" kind is mutually exclusive with both."
    },
    {
